---
import TrafficDrawingHelp from "./TrafficDrawingHelp.astro";
---
<section class="drawing-workspace" aria-labelledby="drawing-heading" id="tm-drawings">
 <p class="eyebrow">DRAWINGS &amp; LAYOUTS</p><h2 id="drawing-heading">Choose how to add your drawing</h2>
 <div class="choices"><a href="#tm-create"><strong>1. Create a drawing</strong><span>Generate a starting layout automatically, then edit it manually. Export DXF or PDF.</span></a><a href="#tm-upload"><strong>2. Upload an existing drawing</strong><span>Choose DXF, DWG, PDF or an image. Preview supported files and download the unchanged original.</span></a></div>
 <p class="draft"><strong>Draft layouts only.</strong> Generated layouts are schematic and not to scale. A competent traffic-management designer must review them against the actual site and applicable standards before use. Symbols are illustrative; calculated distances apply only to the supported rule profile and still need site verification. Signal timings and design approval are not calculated.</p>
 <TrafficDrawingHelp />
 <aside class="training" aria-labelledby="training-heading">
 <h3 id="training-heading">New here? Try training mode</h3>
 <p>A guided tour of the drawing tools, with a separate practice sketch. Your job drawing stays as it is. This teaches the app controls, not traffic-management design competence.</p>
 <button type="button" data-training-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tm-training">Start training mode</button>
 <div id="tm-training" data-training-panel hidden>
 <nav class="toolbar" aria-label="Training steps"><button type="button" data-training-back>Previous</button><span data-training-progress></span><button type="button" data-training-next>Next</button></nav>
 <div tabindex="-1" data-training-content><h4 data-training-title></h4><p data-training-copy></p></div>
 <button type="button" data-training-show>Show this on my job form</button>
 <section data-training-practice hidden aria-label="Separate practice drawing">
 <p><strong>PRACTICE ONLY — imaginary road, no calculated distances.</strong> Choose a symbol and tap the sketch, or use “Add practice symbol”. Try moving a symbol by choosing Select / move, then tapping it and its new position.</p>
 <div class="toolbar"><label>Practice tool<select data-training-tool><option value="cone">Cone</option><option value="sign">Road works sign</option><option value="select">Select / move</option></select></label><button type="button" data-training-add>Add practice symbol</button><button type="button" data-training-reset>Reset practice sketch</button></div>
 <svg data-training-canvas viewBox="0 0 700 260" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="Imaginary practice road. Use Add practice symbol as a keyboard alternative."><rect width="700" height="260" fill="#e6efe9"/><path d="M0 80H700V210H0Z" fill="#626b70"/><path d="M0 145H700" stroke="white" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="25 18"/><text x="16" y="30" font-size="18" fill="#102d23">PRACTICE ONLY — NOT A SITE PLAN</text><g data-training-symbols></g></svg>
 <p data-training-status role="status">Practice sketch ready. Nothing here is saved or exported.</p>
 </section>
 <p class="help">You can close this guide at any time. Practice symbols never go into your job drawing or its exports.</p>
 </div></aside>
 <section id="tm-create" aria-labelledby="create-heading"><h3 id="create-heading">Create a drawing</h3>
 <p>Your layout autosaves in <strong>this browser on this device</strong>, where browser storage is available. It is not saved to your account, sent to our server or attached to a paid work pack. Clearing browser data can erase it. Export DXF or PDF to keep a file; save a project to reopen and edit it later.</p>
 <section class="location-editor" aria-labelledby="location-heading"><h4 id="location-heading">1. Find the job location</h4>
 <p>Search a postcode, road and town, or what3words address. Select the result, adjust the map, then mark the working section on the road centreline below.</p>
 <form data-map-search class="map-search"><label>Job location<input data-map-query maxlength="200" required minlength="3" placeholder="Postcode, Broadmayne Basildon, or ///three.word.address"></label><button type="submit">Find location</button></form>
 <p class="help">Searching sends your location query to Google or what3words. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy</a> · <a href="https://what3words.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">what3words privacy</a> · <a href="https://maps.google.com/help/terms_maps/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Maps terms</a></p><p data-map-status role="status">Checking location search…</p><ul data-map-results class="map-results"></ul>
 <p><a href="#tm-map-controls">Go to the map and its controls ↓</a></p>
 <label>Site layout<select data-map-site><option value="straight">Simple straight road — no affected junctions</option><option value="complex">Slip road / junction / roundabout / affected access</option></select></label>
 <p class="help">A map supplies road context, not a lane survey. Mark junctions, crossings and accesses for review. Automatic generation currently supports verified straight-road cases only; complex sites need manual design on the map. Generated sign locations still need checking for safe siting.</p>
 </section>
 <form data-generator class="generator">
 <h4>2. Describe the job → create an AI drawing</h4>
 <p>Find the location, then mark the fixed <strong>work start</strong> and <strong>work end</strong> on the correct carriageway in the direction of travel. AI will expand beyond this view to inspect the affected upstream and downstream route.</p>
 <label>Describe the traffic-management job<textarea data-ai-description rows="3" maxlength="3000" placeholder="Close lane 1 for drainage works. Keep the other lane open. Describe nearby slip roads, access and any restrictions."></textarea></label>
 <label>Lane to close (numbered from the left in the travel direction)<select data-ai-lane><option value="1">Lane 1</option><option value="2">Lane 2</option></select></label><p>Calculate a core layout for two-way portable signals on a two-lane single carriageway, or one-lane static closures on a 2–4 lane dual carriageway/motorway. Enter surveyed dimensions and the <strong>permanent</strong> speed limit. This is design assistance, not authority approval.</p>
 <div class="generator-fields">
 <label>Road name<input name="roadName" maxlength="80" placeholder="London Road"></label>
 <label>Road / layout<select name="roadType"><option value="single">Single carriageway — two-way signals</option><option value="dual">Dual carriageway — one-lane closure</option><option value="motorway">Motorway — one-lane closure</option></select></label>
 <label>Permanent speed limit (mph)<select name="speed"><option value="20">20</option><option value="30" selected>30</option><option value="40">40</option><option value="50">50</option><option value="60">60</option><option value="70">70</option></select></label>
 <label>Lanes on the modelled carriageway<select name="laneCount"><option value="2">2</option><option value="3">3</option><option value="4">4</option></select></label>
 <label>Closed side in increasing-chainage direction<select name="worksSide"><option value="near">Nearside / left</option><option value="off">Offside / right</option></select></label>
 <div class="lane-measurements"><strong>Lane widths (m)</strong><p class="help">3 m is an assumed starting value, not a measured width. Enter each lane’s site measurement.</p><div data-lane-widths></div><label>Width source<select name="widthSource"><option value="assumed">Assumed — confirm on site</option><option value="surveyed">Surveyed measurements entered</option><option value="map">Map-measured — approximate, confirm</option></select></label><label>Total carriageway width (m)<input name="roadWidth" type="number" min="3" max="25" step="any" readonly required value="6"></label></div>
 <label>Working-space width, excluding safety clearance (m, optional for planning draft)<input name="workWidth" type="number" min="0.5" max="10" step="any" placeholder="Leave blank for a clearly labelled estimate"></label>
 <label>Working-space length (m, optional for planning draft)<input name="worksLength" type="number" min="1" max="1000" step="any" placeholder="Leave blank to estimate between work markers"></label>
 <label>Start of working space — chainage (m)<span class="help field-help">Distance from your chosen reference point to the work. Enter 0 if the work starts at that point; enter 50 if it starts 50 m along the road.</span><input name="worksStart" type="number" min="-10000000" max="10000000" step="any" value="0" required></label>
 </div>
 <label>Proposed works access — distance from work start (m, optional)<input data-ai-access type="number" min="0" max="1000" step="any" placeholder="Leave blank if not requested"></label>
 <label class="generator-check"><input name="hasHardShoulder" type="checkbox"> Hard shoulder present (nearside closures involving it need a separate design)</label>
 <label class="generator-check"><input name="congestion" type="checkbox"> Congestion likely — extend the dual-carriageway advance signing</label>
 <div class="ai-draft-action"><button type="button" data-ai-create disabled>Create planning draft</button><p class="help">AI expands the map to inspect the calculated upstream signing route, works and downstream departure using road and aerial views. Missing measurements remain labelled estimates for review. The editable result is a proposal, not site approval. One request per minute.</p><p data-ai-status role="status">Checking AI drawing availability…</p><div data-ai-review hidden><h4>AI map review</h4><p data-ai-summary></p><ul data-ai-issues></ul></div></div>
 <details class="manual-calculator"><summary>Alternative: standard straight-road calculator</summary>
 <p class="scope-help"><strong>Slip road or junction affected?</strong> Choose the slip-road / junction site layout above and use the manual tools. Leave the confirmation below unticked. Training mode does not unlock automatic design for complex sites.</p>
 <label class="generator-check"><input name="scopeConfirmed" type="checkbox" required> I confirm this is a simple straight-road case without affected junctions, level crossings, guide islands, contraflow, multiple closed lanes or mobile working. A competent designer must check visibility, access, swept paths, queues, pedestrian provision and authority requirements.</label>
 <p>Intermediate portable-signal warning signs are marked provisional for site siting. Temporary speed-limit signing, extra shoulder/access/pedestrian runs, lamps and spare cones are not included in the core quantities. Two-way WAIT HERE separation must not exceed 300 m. Standard lane-closure profiles require 3.6–4 m lanes.</p>
 <button type="submit">Calculate and draw editable draft</button><p data-generator-status role="status">Or use the manual tools below to start from scratch.</p>
 </details>
 </form>
 <p data-cone-count role="status">Cone symbols in current sketch: 0.</p>
 <details class="calculation-details" data-calculation-details hidden><summary>Calculated distances, sign schedule and cone quantities</summary><pre data-calculation-report></pre><button type="button" data-report disabled>Save calculation report</button></details>

 <div class="toolbar"><label>Tool<select data-tool><option value="select">Select / move</option><option value="road">Road</option><option value="cone">Cone</option><option value="barrier">Barrier</option><option value="sign">Sign</option><option value="lights">Traffic lights</option><option value="works">Works area</option><option value="label">Label</option></select></label><label>Sign face<select data-sign-face><option value="generic">Generic warning</option><option value="roadworks">Road works ahead</option><option value="signals">Traffic signals ahead</option><option value="narrows">Road narrows</option><option value="wait">Wait here</option><option value="end">End of road works</option><option value="keep-left">Keep left</option><option value="keep-right">Keep right</option><option value="lane-closure">Lane closure</option></select></label><label>Label / sign text<input data-label maxlength="120" value="Works access"></label><button type="button" data-undo>Undo</button><button type="button" data-delete>Delete selected</button><button type="button" data-clear>New drawing</button></div>
 <p class="help">Drag to draw a road, barrier or works area. Click to place other items. Choose Select / move, then drag an item to reposition it. Select an item to edit its text. The grid is a sketch guide, not a distance scale.</p>
 <div id="tm-map-controls" class="map-controls" aria-label="Map controls"><h4>Map and drawing controls</h4><p class="help">Map zoom changes the area shown. Drawing zoom magnifies the current drawing. Changing the map can clear an existing overlay; save your project first if needed.</p>
 <div class="toolbar"><label>Map view<select data-map-type><option value="roadmap">Road map</option><option value="hybrid">Aerial with road labels</option></select></label><button type="button" data-map-zoom-in>Map +</button><button type="button" data-map-zoom-out>Map −</button><button type="button" data-map-pan="0,-100">North ↑</button><button type="button" data-map-pan="-150,0">West ←</button><button type="button" data-map-pan="150,0">East →</button><button type="button" data-map-pan="0,100">South ↓</button><button type="button" data-map-measure>Measure distance / width</button><button type="button" data-map-ai-mark>Mark work start + work end</button><button type="button" data-map-mark>Mark working section (calculator)</button><button type="button" data-map-feature>Mark junction / access</button><button type="button" data-map-remove>Remove map / start fresh</button></div>
 <p data-map-measurement role="status">Map measurements are approximate. Use Measure distance / width, then tap two points.</p>
 <p data-map-alignment role="status">No working section marked.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="toolbar"><label>Drawing zoom<select data-view-zoom><option value="100">Fit view</option><option value="150">150%</option><option value="200">200%</option><option value="300">300%</option></select></label><button type="button" data-view-pan aria-pressed="false">Pan view</button><span class="help">Use Pan view to scroll a zoomed drawing on your phone.</span></div><div class="canvas-viewport" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable drawing view"><svg data-canvas viewBox="0 0 1000 650" role="img" aria-label="Traffic-management draft drawing canvas" tabindex="0"><defs><pattern id="tm-grid" width="25" height="25" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M 25 0 L 0 0 0 25" fill="none" stroke="#e0e7e5" stroke-width="1"/></pattern></defs><rect width="1000" height="650" fill="url(#tm-grid)"/><image data-map-image x="0" y="0" width="1000" height="650" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><g data-entities></g></svg></div><p class="help">Symbols are illustrative and enlarged for readability. Displaced sign/signal faces use leader lines and dots to show their original marked locations. Map attribution must remain visible. A mapped draft uses the map’s approximate scale, not the old compressed schematic positions.</p>
 <details><summary>Place items using coordinates (keyboard alternative)</summary><div class="coordinates"><label>X<input data-x type="number" min="30" max="950" value="100"></label><label>Y<input data-y type="number" min="30" max="570" value="100"></label><label>End X<input data-x2 type="number" min="30" max="950" value="400"></label><label>End Y<input data-y2 type="number" min="30" max="570" value="200"></label><button type="button" data-add>Add item using selected tool</button><label>Select item<select data-selection><option value="-1">None</option></select></label></div></details>
 <div class="actions"><button type="button" data-pdf>Download drawing PDF</button><button type="button" data-dxf>Export DXF (outlines)</button><button type="button" data-project>Save editable data (.json)</button><label class="file-label">Open project<input data-open-project type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label></div>
 <p data-save-status role="status"></p><p data-drawing-status role="status"></p></section>
 <section id="tm-upload" aria-labelledby="upload-heading"><h3 id="upload-heading">Upload an existing drawing</h3><label>Choose a drawing (maximum 20 MB)<input data-upload type="file" accept=".dxf,.dwg,.pdf,.png,.jpg,.jpeg,.webp,.gif,.bmp"></label>
 <p>Files stay in this tab’s memory and are <strong>not uploaded to a server or saved to your account</strong>. Reloading or closing the tab removes them. Keep your own original. Uploading does not attach a drawing to checkout.</p>
 <p>DXF: basic ASCII LINE, CIRCLE, TEXT and straight LWPOLYLINE previews only; other entities, blocks, dimensions, styling and external references may be missing. PDF viewing depends on your browser. PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF and BMP images can be previewed. <strong>DWG cannot be viewed or edited here</strong>: download the original and use a compatible CAD viewer, or export DXF, PDF or an image from your CAD application for preview.</p>
 <p data-upload-status role="status"></p><a data-original hidden>Download original</a><div data-preview class="preview"></div></section>
 <p class="work-pack-link">Need the accompanying work pack? <a href="#tm-form">Continue to the existing work-pack form ↓</a></p>
</section>
<script>import { bindTrafficDrawing } from '../lib/traffic-management/client';bindTrafficDrawing();import { bindTrafficTraining } from '../lib/traffic-management/training';bindTrafficTraining();</script>
<style>
.drawing-workspace textarea{display:block;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;font:inherit;padding:10px;border:1px solid #9eb4a8;border-radius:5px}.ai-draft-action{padding:16px;border:2px solid #126747;background:#f1f8f4;margin:18px 0}.manual-calculator{margin:16px 0}.manual-calculator summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:800}

.training{border:2px solid #126747;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;margin:20px 0;background:#f1f8f4}.training h3{margin-top:0}.training h4{font-size:21px}.training [data-training-canvas]{display:block;width:100%;border:1px solid #9eb4a8;touch-action:pan-y}.field-help{display:block;font-weight:400;margin:6px 0}.scope-help{border-left:4px solid #126747;padding:12px;background:white}.drawing-workspace :global(.training-highlight){outline:3px solid #126747;outline-offset:5px}

.canvas-viewport{width:100%;overflow:auto;max-height:760px;border:1px solid #9eb4a8}.location-editor{padding:20px;border:2px solid #9eb4a8;border-radius:8px}.location-editor h4{font-size:22px;margin:0}.map-search{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:end;gap:12px}.map-search label{flex:1;min-width:180px}.map-search input{width:100%}.map-results{padding-left:0;list-style:none}.map-results li{margin:8px 0}.map-results button{max-width:100%;text-align:left}.lane-measurements{padding:12px;border:1px solid #9eb4a8}.drawing-workspace{background:#fff;color:#102d23;padding:30px;border-radius:12px;margin:28px 0 36px}.drawing-workspace h2{font-size:30px;margin-top:0}.drawing-workspace h3{font-size:25px;color:#126747}.choices{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.choices a{display:block;border:2px solid #f57f20;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;text-decoration:none;background:#fff9f2;color:inherit}.choices strong,.choices span{display:block}.choices strong{font-size:21px;margin-bottom:8px}.draft{border-left:5px solid #f57f20;padding:16px;background:#fff6ec}.generator{border:2px solid #f57f20;background:#fff9f2;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;margin:22px 0}.generator h4{font-size:22px;margin:0}.generator-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:15px;margin:18px 0}.generator-fields input,.generator-fields select{width:100%}.generator-check{display:flex!important;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin:14px 0}.generator-check input{margin-top:5px;flex-shrink:0}.calculation-details{border:1px solid #bfd0c6;border-radius:6px;padding:14px}.calculation-details pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;max-height:500px;overflow:auto}.toolbar,.actions,.coordinates{display:flex;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:16px 0}.drawing-workspace label{font-weight:750;display:block}.drawing-workspace input,.drawing-workspace select{display:block;font:inherit;box-sizing:border-box;max-width:100%;padding:9px;border:1px solid #9eb4a8;border-radius:5px}.drawing-workspace button{font:inherit;font-weight:800;background:#f57f20;color:#071421;border:0;border-radius:5px;padding:11px 15px;cursor:pointer}.drawing-workspace button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}.drawing-workspace :focus-visible{outline:3px solid #126747;outline-offset:3px}.drawing-workspace svg[data-canvas]{width:100%;display:block;background:white;border:1px solid #9eb4a8;touch-action:none}.help{font-size:15px}.coordinates input{width:100px}.preview{margin-top:16px}.preview :global(img),.preview :global(svg){display:block;max-width:100%;max-height:650px;margin:auto;background:#fff}.preview :global(iframe){width:100%;height:600px;border:1px solid #9eb4a8}.file-label{font-size:14px}.file-label input{font-size:13px}.drawing-workspace section{scroll-margin-top:24px;margin-top:28px}.work-pack-link{border-top:1px solid #bfd0c6;margin-top:24px;padding-top:20px}.drawing-workspace [hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:720px){.choices{grid-template-columns:1fr}.drawing-workspace{padding:18px}.toolbar>*{max-width:100%}.drawing-workspace input[type=file]{width:100%}}
</style>
